title: Small formats, read one way
intro: A field typed in a small format, like the gems a Match-3 level asks for, reads the same in the editor and the game, and a part that doesn't read is flagged.
project: Empty | Formats

chapter: A goal that doesn't read | The game says so
create: Empty
rename: Board
add: MatchBoard
set: MatchBoard.Collect = 0:3, oops
say: A Match-3 board's Collect field is typed as tile and count pairs. Here the second pair is not a pair.
play
expectproblem: MatchBoard = oops
explain: component:MatchBoard | The flag | The game reads Collect the same way the Inspector's rows do, so the part that doesn't read is flagged on the board while the game plays, once, rather than skipped without a word.
stop
set: MatchBoard.Collect = 0:3, 2:5
play
expectproblem: MatchBoard = none
say: Written as pairs, both read, and nothing is flagged.
stop
